From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:59:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Feature-gate the terminal-capability query behind `query`

rustix is declared unconditionally for cfg(not(windows)), which
includes wasm32-unknown-unknown, and there its errno dependency
hard-errors with "The target OS is \"unknown\" or \"none\", so it's
unsupported by the errno crate". So the crate cannot be built for
wasm at all, even though halfblocks needs nothing but a Buffer and
kitty/iterm2 need nothing but base64.

Nothing outside the stdio query wants a terminal: the query owns
enable_raw_mode, font_size_fallback, query_stdio_capabilities,
interpret_parser_responses, query_with_timeout and the two Errno
conversions. Gate exactly those. Picker::from_fontsize, already
documented as "the only way to create a picker on windows", covers
every caller that knows its cell size by other means.

The feature is in `default`, so this is not a breaking change for
anyone building for a real terminal.
---
 Cargo.toml    |  7 +++++++
 src/errors.rs |  2 ++
 src/picker.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

